card c04
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: A decay chain
figure: chain-figure
figure_at: 2

body:
    A [[decay-chain|decay chain]] is a sequence of radioactive decays: one nucleus changes into another, which may decay again. It ends only when a stable nucleus is reached, because a stable nucleus has nothing left to change into.

card c08
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l4-order-chain

card c11
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l4-choice-finished

card c10
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Nothing vanishes
figure: chain-zoom-out
figure_at: 1

body:
    Look at what each step does. A decay does not make an atom disappear. It changes the nucleus into a different nucleus, and that different nucleus is what is left behind. One unstable nucleus can start a whole chain of these changes.

card c06
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l4-tom-vanish
connected: true

card c07
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l4-tom-different

card c12
kind: teach
type: explain
tier: deeper
scored: 0
title: Go deeper: real chains
figure: real-chains
figure_at: 2

body:
    Real decay chains exist in nature. The uranium-238 chain ends in stable lead-206. The thorium-232 chain ends in stable lead-208. Some steps can branch in more than one way. There is nothing to memorise.
